# Scacelith - Slovenčina
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals have three forms:
# one (1)|few (2-4)|other (0, 5 and more).
# Register: formal "vy" (lower case mid-sentence), as Microsoft and Apple Slovak software; instructions
# in the formal imperative ("Vyberte", "Zadajte"), buttons, menu entries and commands in the infinitive
# ("Uložiť", "Vzdať partiu"); sentence case, never Title Case. Titles are in capitals (the title face
# is an inscriptional capital face).
# The player's gender is unknown: the formal past tense is plural and neutral ("vyhrali ste"), but no
# adjective, passive participle or "sám/sami" about the player ("ste prihlásený"): nouns or impersonal
# phrasing instead ("Odhlásenie prebehlo", "Kódy mám uložené").
# Chess terms of the Slovak chess federation and the Slovak FIDE Laws: pešiak, jazdec, strelec, veža,
# dáma, kráľ; partiár (scoresheet), tempo hry (time control), rating, remíza, nemožný ťah (illegal
# move), rozhodca (arbiter), polťah (ply). White / Black as players: "biely" / "čierny".
# Keep the sections: other parts of the game add their keys in sections of their own.

